      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COUSR03C DELETE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COUSR03C's delete-user CICS transaction by mocking
      *  ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS API: the
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator emits in
      *  place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND MAP, READ
      *  DATASET, DELETE DATASET, XCTL, RETURN).  The DFHEI1 entry
      *  point is the single ABI seam between the production COBOL
      *  program and the CICS runtime; mocking it intercepts every
      *  CICS service call without requiring a live CICS region.
      *
      *  Internal COUSR03C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every TESTCASE
      *  exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM so the
      *  testsuite asserts against side effects of actual production-
      *  code execution (per the user directive in AAP Section 0.10.1
      *  -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports the mock-types
      *  CALL, PARA, PARAGRAPH, and SECTION (verified against the
      *  Keywords class in cobol-check-0.2.16.jar).  At link time on
      *  z/OS the CICS translator (DFHECP1$) rewrites every
      *      EXEC CICS <verb> ... END-EXEC.
      *  into a sequence whose terminal statement is
      *      CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block> ...
      *  so MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is the equivalent intercept point.
      *  Off-platform (GnuCOBOL on Linux) the same mock applies once
      *  the CICS translator runs as a precompile pass; until that
      *  pass exists in this repository the production EXEC CICS
      *  verbs reach the linker as-is, the merged binary fails to
      *  compile (a known infrastructure gap covered by AAP Section
      *  6.6.3.1's documented "manual testing only" baseline), and
      *  the mock simply registers without firing.  The testsuite
      *  itself is forward-compatible: when a CICS translator pass
      *  is added, the same .cut file exercises every CICS boundary
      *  through this mock.
      *
      *  Mock placement rule
      *  -------------------
      *  Each MOCK is declared INSIDE its corresponding TESTCASE
      *  block (after the TESTCASE keyword) so the cobol-check parser
      *  binds the mock's Local scope to the CURRENT testcase name.
      *  This guarantees that the matching VERIFY clause inside the
      *  same testcase resolves to the testcase-specific Local mock
      *  with the testcase-specific mock body.  This mirrors the
      *  exemplar pattern in tests/cobol-check/CBSTM03A.cut.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          = SPACES; production substitutes the default 'COSGN00C'
      *          target, captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields, and issues XCTL.
      *    TC2 - PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS; production resets
      *          USRIDINL to -1 and clears USRIDINI, FNAMEI, LNAMEI,
      *          USRTYPEI, and WS-MESSAGE to SPACES.  No CICS verbs;
      *          purely WORKING-STORAGE side effects.
      *    TC3 - PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with USRIDINI = SPACES;
      *          production EVALUATE TRUE matches the empty-user-id
      *          branch, sets WS-ERR-FLG ON, and short-circuits before
      *          any READ DATASET dispatches.
      *    TC4 - PERFORM DELETE-USER-INFO with USRIDINI = SPACES;
      *          production again short-circuits via the empty-user-id
      *          guard, leaving WS-ERR-FLG ON without invoking either
      *          READ-USER-SEC-FILE or DELETE-USER-SEC-FILE.
      *    TC5 - PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN; production performs
      *          INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS first (clearing the BMS map)
      *          and then SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN.  The test asserts the
      *          INITIALIZE side effects observable in WORKING-STORAGE.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file plan for COUSR03C
      *    app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl lines 142-169 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl lines 174-192 (DELETE-USER-INFO)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl lines 197-208 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl lines 341-344 (CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR03C.cbl lines 349-356 (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy            (SEC-USER-DATA layout)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COUSR03.CPY         (COUSR3AI / COUSR3AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      ******************************************************************
      *
      *  DFHEI1 fail-loudly safety net (QA CP4 Phase 5.2 anchor).
      *  Runner-script Step 5 (linux_gnucobol_run_tests) injects
      *  the actual EXTERNAL field declarations into merged WS;
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16 drops the directive below silently --
      *  intended -- and BEFORE-EACH resets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-
      *  CALLED so a stub-fired condition is assertable per test.
      ******************************************************************
       COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.

       TESTSUITE 'COUSR03C DELETE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the application working-storage
      *  fields and shared structures the production code reads or
      *  writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        - WS-PGMNAME, WS-TRANID, WS-MESSAGE,
      *                          WS-USRSEC-FILE, WS-ERR-FLG, WS-RESP-CD,
      *                          WS-REAS-CD, WS-USR-MODIFIED.  After
      *                          INITIALIZE re-applies VALUE clauses,
      *                          WS-PGMNAME = 'COUSR03C', WS-TRANID =
      *                          'CU03', and WS-ERR-FLG = 'N' (per
      *                          production lines 36-42).
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   - whole COCOM01Y group plus the
      *                          CDEMO-CU03-INFO extension fields
      *    SEC-USER-DATA       - CSUSR01Y group (SEC-USR-ID,
      *                          SEC-USR-FNAME, SEC-USR-LNAME,
      *                          SEC-USR-PWD, SEC-USR-TYPE)
      *    COUSR3AI            - BMS input map (USRIDINI, FNAMEI,
      *                          LNAMEI, USRTYPEI, ERRMSGI ...)
      *    RETURN-CODE         - implicit special register reset for
      *                          deterministic post-test inspection
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  ADMIN001 admin-role identity (the only test user permitted
      *  by AAP Section 0.10.2 for this transaction) so each TESTCASE
      *  starts from the routed-by-COADM01C state that production
      *  COUSR03C expects.  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to the
      *  upstream admin menu so the RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN paragraph
      *  has a non-empty origin to reflect back into the COMMAREA.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE SEC-USER-DATA
            INITIALIZE COUSR3AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'N'        TO WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED
            MOVE 'ADMIN001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'A'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COADM01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CA00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 197-208).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 111-118) and of the EIBCALEN = 0
      *  initial-entry branch (production lines 90-92), so it is the
      *  PF3 "cancel" path's final hop before XCTL.
      *
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 199)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 200)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 202)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 203)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 204)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 205)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 206)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 207)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 208)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in BEFORE-EACH;
      *                       INITIALIZE on a PIC X group fills with
      *                       spaces, satisfying the WHEN OR SPACES
      *                       half of the line-199 IF).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COADM01C' (BEFORE-EACH default; will
      *                       be overwritten by line-203 production
      *                       MOVE -- the test asserts the SIDE EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 200 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side effect,
      *                 does NOT recompute or paraphrase the IF logic)
      *    'COUSR03C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'COUSR03C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 203
      *    'CU03'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CU03'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 202
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR03C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COUSR03C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CU03'
            EXPECT WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears the map and message
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (production lines 349-356).
      *  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM
      *  statements; it is the cleanest test target in COUSR03C.  The
      *  paragraph executes:
      *
      *    MOVE -1     TO USRIDINL OF COUSR3AI                (line 351)
      *    MOVE SPACES TO USRIDINI OF COUSR3AI                (line 352)
      *                   FNAMEI   OF COUSR3AI                (line 353)
      *                   LNAMEI   OF COUSR3AI                (line 354)
      *                   USRTYPEI OF COUSR3AI                (line 355)
      *                   WS-MESSAGE.                         (line 356)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude (after BEFORE-EACH
      *  zeroes the structures): seed USRIDINI / FNAMEI / LNAMEI /
      *  USRTYPEI / WS-MESSAGE with non-empty markers so the test
      *  proves the production MOVE TO SPACES actually overwrites
      *  them.  Without these seeds the BEFORE-EACH initial state
      *  would already be SPACES and the test would not distinguish
      *  the production paragraph's effect from baseline.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES     - production literal MOVE'd by lines 352-356;
      *                 the test asserts the side effect (does NOT
      *                 reimplement the MOVE)
      *
      *  A MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so the testcase can also
      *  ASSERT (via VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES) the production
      *  invariant that INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS NEVER reaches a CICS
      *  service call.  This is a meaningful production-behavior
      *  assertion: a regression that introduces an EXEC CICS verb
      *  inside this paragraph would inflate the mock count and
      *  fail the VERIFY clause.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR03C INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS clears USRIDINI WS-MSG'
            MOVE 'OLDUSER ' TO USRIDINI OF COUSR3AI
            MOVE 'OLDFNAME            ' TO FNAMEI OF COUSR3AI
            MOVE 'OLDLNAME            ' TO LNAMEI OF COUSR3AI
            MOVE 'X' TO USRTYPEI OF COUSR3AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS
            EXPECT USRIDINI OF COUSR3AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT FNAMEI OF COUSR3AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT LNAMEI OF COUSR3AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT USRTYPEI OF COUSR3AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty user ID
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 142-169) with
      *  USRIDINI cleared by INITIALIZE COUSR3AI in BEFORE-EACH (so
      *  the field holds LOW-VALUES, which the production EVALUATE
      *  TRUE WHEN clause matches alongside SPACES).  The production
      *  EVALUATE block executes:
      *
      *    EVALUATE TRUE
      *        WHEN USRIDINI = SPACES OR LOW-VALUES        (line 145)
      *            MOVE 'Y' TO WS-ERR-FLG                  (line 146)
      *            MOVE 'User ID can NOT be empty...' TO WS-MESSAGE
      *            MOVE -1  TO USRIDINL                    (line 149)
      *            PERFORM SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN              (line 150)
      *        WHEN OTHER
      *            MOVE -1 TO USRIDINL                     (line 152)
      *            CONTINUE                                (line 153)
      *    END-EVALUATE                                    (line 154)
      *
      *  After the EVALUATE, the IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 156
      *  is FALSE because production set WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y', so the
      *  paragraph short-circuits without ever issuing READ-USER-SEC-
      *  FILE.  This is the production-mandated invariant: validation
      *  failures gate CICS / VSAM I/O.
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN's
      *  EXEC CICS SEND can be intercepted (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1') without spawning any real
      *  3270 traffic; the mock body is CONTINUE so the production
      *  flow returns to PROCESS-ENTER-KEY without side effects.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 146 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute or
      *          paraphrase the EVALUATE logic)
      *    -1  - USRIDINL flipped by production line 149 (negative
      *          length signals "cursor here" to the BMS layer)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR03C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects empty user ID'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT USRIDINL OF COUSR3AI NOT = 0
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- DELETE-USER-INFO short-circuits on empty user ID
      *
      *  Drives DELETE-USER-INFO (production lines 174-192) with
      *  USRIDINI cleared by INITIALIZE COUSR3AI in BEFORE-EACH.
      *  The paragraph's EVALUATE block (lines 176-186) mirrors
      *  PROCESS-ENTER-KEY's: a SPACES / LOW-VALUES user ID flips
      *  WS-ERR-FLG = 'Y' and short-circuits before the IF NOT
      *  ERR-FLG-ON guard at line 188 admits the READ + DELETE pair.
      *
      *  This testcase complements TC3 by proving the same input-
      *  validation guard is enforced by both transaction-entry
      *  paragraphs, not just PROCESS-ENTER-KEY.  Without this
      *  redundant test, a regression that removes the SPACES /
      *  LOW-VALUES check from DELETE-USER-INFO (line 177) would
      *  go undetected because PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (line 145) still
      *  catches the same case.  The user directive in AAP Section
      *  0.10.1 -- "exercise paragraphs LIVE via PERFORM" -- requires
      *  separate coverage for each paragraph.
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared as a defensive measure
      *  so that, in the regression scenario where production starts
      *  reaching SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN (or, worse, READ-USER-SEC-FILE),
      *  the EXEC CICS verbs are intercepted instead of crashing the
      *  test harness.  The VERIFY clause asserts the LOW BOUND on
      *  the mock invocation count: the assertion is satisfied
      *  whether production reaches zero, one, or two SEND verbs
      *  (the production paragraph performs SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN
      *  exactly once on the validation-failure path, line 182).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'Y' - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 178 (test
      *          asserts the side effect, does NOT recompute the
      *          EVALUATE logic)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR03C DELETE-USER-INFO rejects empty user ID'
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM DELETE-USER-INFO
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN orchestrates INITIALIZE + SEND
      *
      *  Drives CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN (production lines 341-344).
      *  The paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF4
      *  branch (line 119-120) and executes:
      *
      *    PERFORM INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS.            (line 343)
      *    PERFORM SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN.               (line 344)
      *
      *  PERFORM 1: INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS (lines 349-356) -- the
      *  same paragraph TC2 covers in isolation.  Here we assert
      *  the SAME side effects manifest when the orchestrator runs
      *  end-to-end, proving the orchestrator does not bypass or
      *  short-circuit its inner PERFORMs.
      *
      *  PERFORM 2: SEND-USRDEL-SCREEN (lines 213-225) -- performs
      *  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO and then issues EXEC CICS SEND MAP.
      *  The mock intercepts the SEND verb (after CICS translator
      *  rewrites it to CALL 'DFHEI1') so no 3270 traffic is
      *  generated.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC5 prelude: seed the same
      *  fields TC2 seeds, plus WS-MESSAGE, so the test proves that
      *  CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN's first PERFORM (INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS)
      *  reaches and executes its MOVE-TO-SPACES statements.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by INITIALIZE-ALL-
      *             FIELDS lines 352-356; the test asserts the side
      *             effect (does NOT reimplement the MOVE)
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR03C CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN clears USRIDINI WS-MSG'
            MOVE 'OLDUSER ' TO USRIDINI OF COUSR3AI
            MOVE 'STALE MESSAGE FROM PRIOR FIXTURE' TO WS-MESSAGE
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM CLEAR-CURRENT-SCREEN
            EXPECT USRIDINI OF COUSR3AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COUSR03C DELETE USER ADMIN TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
